-- title:
--   Higman–Neumann–Neumann embedding theorem for an HNN extension with finitely many stable letters
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be a group (`H : Type u` with `[Group H]`) and let `I : Type v` be a finite index type (`[Fintype I]`). For each $i \in I$ let $A_i, B_i \le H$ be subgroups (`A B : I → Subgroup H`) and let $\varphi_i : A_i \to B_i$ be a group isomorphism (`φ : ∀ i, A i ≃* B i`). The multiple HNN extension
--   $$\mathrm{HNN}(H; A_i \xrightarrow{\varphi_i} B_i) \;=\; \bigl\langle\, H,\ t_i\ (i \in I) \;\bigm|\; t_i\, a\, t_i^{-1} = \varphi_i(a) \ \ (i \in I,\ a \in A_i) \,\bigr\rangle$$
--   is `Extension A B φ`: the free product of $H$ with the free group on $I$ (`Monoid.Coprod H (FreeGroup I)`) divided by the congruence `con A B φ` generated by the relations $t_i\,a = \varphi_i(a)\,t_i$ for $i \in I$ and $a \in A_i$, with the quotient group structure `instGroupExtension`. The homomorphism `of A B φ : H →* Extension A B φ` sends $h \in H$ to its class.
--
--   Then `of A B φ` is injective: $H$ embeds in the multiple HNN extension.
--
--   For a single stable letter this is the embedding theorem of Higman, Neumann and Neumann (1949). With finitely many letters it follows by adding the letters one at a time.
--
--   Lean: `OAI.KaplanskyCounterexample.MultipleHNN.of_injective`, OpenAI's theorem of that name in `lean/OAI/RingTheory/DirectFiniteness/MultiHNN.lean`. `con`, `Extension`, `instGroupExtension` and `of` come from the definitions bundle `OAIQWKAPHNN`, which contains only OpenAI's multiple-HNN construction and imports nothing but Mathlib.
-- source:
--   G. Higman, B. H. Neumann and H. Neumann, Embedding theorems for groups, J. London Math. Soc. 24 (1949), 247–254 (the HNN construction and its embedding theorem). Lean proof: OpenAI, A Counterexample to Kaplansky's Direct-Finiteness Conjecture in Characteristic Two, OpenAI Math Release, September 23, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math (result family 197; paper: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-Counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-Direct-Finiteness-Conjecture-in-Characteristic-Two-September-23-2026/paper.pdf; Apache License 2.0); Lean: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/RingTheory/DirectFiniteness/MultiHNN.lean (declaration OAI.KaplanskyCounterexample.MultipleHNN.of_injective)

